      "title": "Victorian House AI Generation",
      "category": "ai",
      "caption": "AI / ARCHITECTURAL RECONSTRUCTION",
      "description": "Starting from a single street photo of a San Francisco Victorian, I rebuilt the house and its block in 3D with Claude driving Blender, plus a few generative image tools for skies, reflections and ornament detail. I matched the camera to the photo first, then layered in light, materials, trees and all the small imperfections that make a street feel lived in. A lot of side-by-side comparisons, a lot of tiny fixes, and one facade that had to hold up next to the real thing.",
